      <h3
        class="text-xl font-bold mb-2"
      >
        Hue Shift
      </h3>
      <div
        class="space-y-3"
      >
        <p>
          Colors rarely sit on a single hue across a full range, and pinning them there is part of what makes a scale feel synthetic. A small, controlled shift adds depth: cool the highlights a few degrees, warm the shadows, and the scale gains a sense of light moving through it. Keep it subtle — enough to feel, not enough to turn your blue into teal at one end.
        </p>
